,"scientificName":"Loxodonta africana (Blumenbach, 1797)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2435350},"ottId":541936,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Loxodonta africana","synonyms":["Elephas africana","Elephas capensis","Loxodonta africana africana"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The African bush elephant (Loxodonta africana), also known as the African savanna elephant, is a species of elephant native to sub-Saharan Africa and the largest living terrestrial animal, with fully grown bulls reaching an average shoulder height of 3.04–3.36 m (10.0–11.0 ft) and a body mass of 5.2–6.9 t (5.7–7.6 short tons); the largest recorded specimen had a shoulder height of 3.96 m (13.0 ft) and an estimated body mass of 10.4 t (11.5 short tons). It is characterised by its long prehensile trunk with two finger-like processes; a concave back; large ears which help reduce body heat; and sturdy tusks that are noticeably curved.","revisionId":1375310743,"title":"African bush elephant","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_bush_elephant","wikidataId":"Q36557"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Monk Parakeets","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Monk and Cliff Parakeets","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"parakeet","source":"The Paleobiology Database"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Myiopsitta","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Myiopsitta Bonaparte, 1854","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2479406},"ottId":547248,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Myiopsitta","synonyms":["Myopsitta","Myopsittacus"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Myiopsitta is a genus of parrots in the family Psittacidae. They are native to southeastern South America, from Bolivia and southern Brazil, south to central Argentina.","revisionId":1333841481,"title":"Myiopsitta","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myiopsitta","wikidataId":"Q10795783"}},{"commonNames":[],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Oreopholus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Oreopholus Jardine & Selby, 1835