 ape.","revisionId":1362170396,"title":"Proconsul africanus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proconsul_africanus","wikidataId":"Q1983461"}},{"commonNames":[],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Heliadornis","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Heliadornis Olson, 1985","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":4848880},"ottId":4131184,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Heliadornis","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Heliadornis is a genus of prehistoric seabirds related to modern tropicbirds, but native to temperate climates. They lived in the Miocene.","revisionId":1192933677,"title":"Heliadornis","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliadornis","wikidataId":"Q30693740"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Austral storm petrel","source":"Wikipedia"}],"ottId":5852528,"scientificName":"Oceanitinae","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Austral storm petrels, or southern storm petrels, are seabirds in the family Oceanitidae, part of the order Procellariiformes. These smallest of seabirds feed on planktonic crustaceans and small fish picked from the surface, typically while hovering.","revisionId":1370869694,"title":"Austral storm petrel","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austral_storm_petrel","wikidataId":"Q21296168"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Humboldt’s Squirrel Monkey","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"albigena","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Colombian Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Humboldt's Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Colombian Squirrel Monkey (albigena)","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Saimiri cassiquiarensis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Saimiri cassiquiarensis (Lesson, 1840)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":7576788},"ottId":6145200,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Saimiri cassiquiarensis","synonyms":["Simia sciurea cassiquiarensis"],"wikipedia"